-- title:
--   From an interior integrand estimate to the full Euler main term
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ne0$, $k\ge2$, and $R\ge2$, and fix a smooth sieve cutoff $\chi$, selected CFZ pattern $e$, and natural parameters $w,b$. Assume $w$ bounds the exceptional primes of the full CFZ affine-form family and $\operatorname{primorial}(w)$ is coprime to $b$. Let $\delta\ge0$ and $T\in\mathbb R$. If the scaled complete Euler integrand differs pointwise from the archimedean baseline by at most $\delta$ times its norm inside the selected Fourier box of radius $T$, then the norm of the Fourier main term minus $1$ is at most $\delta$ times the full integral of the baseline norm, plus the scaled complete-Euler tail norm at $T$, plus the norm of the baseline integral outside that box.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e/src/latest/Wikipedia/GreenTao/Sieve/CFZCanonicalCompleteMainTermBridge.lean#L658-L831

